"""Regression tests for the constitutional law.

The layer invariant is the one rule the whole system rests on, so it gets a
test that fails loudly rather than a comment asking people to be careful.
Each case builds a throwaway knowledge base, runs bin/wb-validate against it,
and asserts both the exit status and that the diagnostic actually names the
problem — an error that fires for the wrong reason is not a passing test.

Usage:  tests/test-invariant [-v]

Standard library only. Exit 0 when every case passes.
"""

